module

public import WeilConjectures.Blowup.Affine.Functoriality

/-!

# Generation of the base-changed blow-up chart

Let `φ : A →+* B` be a ring homomorphism, `I ⊆ A` an ideal and `J = I·B` its extension.
For a degree-one element `x` of the Rees algebra of `I`, the chart ring
`Away (reesGrading J) (φ(x))` of the blow-up of `J` is generated, as a ring, by the
images of the two canonical maps out of the chart data of the blow-up of `I`:

- the structure map `B →+* Away (reesGrading J) (φ(x))`
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.AffineBlowup.awayAlgebraMap`), and
- the functoriality map
  `Away (reesGrading I) x →+* Away (reesGrading J) (φ(x))`
  (`HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map` along `AlgebraicGeometry.reesGrading.hom`).

This is the algebraic heart of the chart-wise closed immersion
`Bl_J(Spec B) ⟶ Spec B ×_{Spec A} Bl_I(Spec A)` of Stacks Project Tag 080E: a fraction
`y/φ(a)ⁿ` with `y ∈ Jⁿ = Iⁿ·B` decomposes as a `B`-linear combination of fractions
`φ(z)/φ(a)ⁿ` with `z ∈ Iⁿ`, each of which comes from the chart ring of `Bl_I`.

## Main results

- `AlgebraicGeometry.AffineBlowup.closure_range_awayAlgebraMap_union_range_awayMap`

## Blueprint

Part of `thm:nagata-strict-transform-is-blowup` (Stacks Project Tag 080E), affine chart
layer.

-/

@[expose] public section

noncomputable section

universe u

open CategoryTheory HomogeneousLocalization

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.AffineBlowup

variable {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] {I : Ideal A} {J : Ideal B}

/-- **The base-changed blow-up chart is generated by the two canonical images**
(Stacks Project Tag 080E, affine chart layer; blueprint:
`thm:nagata-strict-transform-is-blowup`): for a ring homomorphism `φ : A →+* B` with
`I.map φ = J` and a degree-one element `x` of the Rees algebra of `I`, the chart ring
of the blow-up of `J` at `φ(x)` is generated as a ring by the image of `B` and the
image of the chart ring of the blow-up of `I` at `x`. -/
theorem closure_range_awayAlgebraMap_union_range_awayMap
    (φ : A →+* B) (h : I.map φ = J) (x : reesAlgebra I) (hx : x ∈ reesGrading I 1) :
    Subring.closure
        (Set.range (awayAlgebraMap J (reesGrading.hom φ h x)) ∪
          Set.range (HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map (reesGrading.hom φ h) x)) = ⊤ := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.AffineBlowup
